== results: benchmark/results/20260926T194921Z-8be7ca6-multihost-L2
# Phase 7B Level 2: T 3-of-5 across 5 AWS regions

> LABEL: Level 2: 5 regions, one provider (AWS), one account, one operator, one build, one dealer; real WAN, RTT measured per signer (TCP connect from the coordinator host), no netem. Coordinator aws:ap-south-1a:m7i-flex.large; signers: 1=aws:ap-south-1b:t3.micro 2=aws:ap-southeast-1a:t3.micro 3=aws:ap-northeast-1a:t3.micro 4=aws:eu-central-1a:t3.micro 5=aws:us-east-1a:t3.micro . Tags: <scenario>-<strategy>-<fanout>; far-quorum = signers 1 2 (lowest measured RTT) stopped. Configured netem column is always 0 (no netem); rows are labelled by the MEASURED quorum RTT during the run.

Generated by `benchmark/summarize` from the raw CSVs and RTT measurements listed at the end. Latencies in ms; percentiles are nearest-rank over successful requests; **goodput** = successful requests / (last end − first start over ALL requests of the run); offered = all completed requests over the same window; failed p95 = p95 latency of failed requests. **Measured quorum RTT** = 3rd-smallest per-signer RTT from the coordinator host (a 3-of-5 quorum waits for the 3rd share); the configured netem delay is a knob, not a measurement (NOTES N45). Every configuration run is listed, including the worst.

