## Pod scale-up (B0 vs B1 vs T)

A Deployment of pause pods, each with one projected service account token (automount off), scaled from 0 on an otherwise idle cluster. **Time to Ready** = from the `kubectl scale` command until `readyReplicas` equals the target (median of repetitions, [min–max]). **Token latency** = kube-apiserver audit `stageTimestamp − requestReceivedTimestamp` of each kubelet TokenRequest, pooled over the repetitions (nearest-rank). **Coordinator** columns (T only) come from the coordinators' `signed` / `sign failed` log lines; **signer 503s** counts `HTTP 503` (signer at capacity/shed) in those lines. CPU = host busy % over the scale window.

